    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-09-01T09:16:42+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-01T09:16:42+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-31T23:46:42Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-31T23:46:42Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A cold front is expected to move across SA today as a high pressure system moves further east of Australia. Another high pressure ridge will move across the north of the state on Wednesday and Thursday and another cold front will slip across the southeast of SA early Thursday. The ridge will move eastwards early Friday then another trough and cold front will move over SA during the day.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW011" description="Eastern Eyre Peninsula" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-09-01T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-02T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-31T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-01T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Medium chance of showers, most likely in the late afternoon and evening. Winds north to northwesterly 30 to 45 km/h turning west to southwesterly 15 to 25 km/h in the afternoon. Daytime maximum temperatures in the low to mid 20s.</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:30am to 3:00pm, UV Index predicted to reach 6 [High]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-09-02T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-03T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-01T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-02T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Cloudy. Slight chance of a shower, most likely in the early morning. Winds southwesterly 15 to 20 km/h tending westerly 15 to 25 km/h in the middle of the day. Overnight temperatures falling to between 9 and 12 with daytime temperatures reaching between 17 and 20.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-09-03T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-04T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-02T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-03T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Medium chance of showers in the south, slight chance elsewhere. Winds west to northwesterly 15 to 25 km/h tending west to southwesterly 15 to 20 km/h during the afternoon then becoming light during the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to around 8 with daytime temperatures reaching between 18 and 21.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-09-04T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-05T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-03T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-04T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Cloudy. Very high chance of showers, most likely in the morning. Winds northerly 20 to 30 km/h turning west to northwesterly 15 to 25 km/h during the afternoon. Overnight temperatures falling to around 10 with daytime temperatures reaching the low 20s.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
